+# MiMo-V2.5-Pro MLX Text Backbone Track A
+
+## Scope
+
+Track A introduces reviewable scaffolding for `XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5-Pro` as a text-only, agentic, long-context causal LM target in exo/MLX. The target model card and validation surface must remain text-only: no image, video, audio, or omnimodal capability is introduced for Pro.
+
+## Tokenizer/config inventory smoke rung
+
+The tokenizer/config inventory smoke rung is a pre-inference, metadata-only check for the MiMo-V2.5-Pro Track A scaffold. Its purpose is to confirm that lightweight repository metadata and local manifest-style files are present and internally coherent before any future MLX load path is allowed to proceed.
+
+Allowed inputs for this smoke rung are limited to lightweight metadata files such as:
+
+- `config.json` fields that identify the text causal-LM architecture, long-context limits, FP8 E4M3 quantization metadata, MoE routing/expert metadata, hybrid full/SWA attention metadata, and disabled MTP state.
+- tokenizer metadata files and tokenizer configuration files, for example `tokenizer.json`, `tokenizer_config.json`, `special_tokens_map.json`, or equivalent local repository metadata.
+- generation metadata files such as `generation_config.json` when present; these may define text-only defaults such as BOS/EOS/pad token IDs, temperature/top-p/top-k defaults, repetition penalties, max-new-token defaults, and chat stop-token behavior, but must not imply media preprocessing or non-text decoders.
+- repository index or manifest files such as `model.safetensors.index.json`, shard manifests, or MLX conversion metadata when present; this rung may inspect only names, declared tensor keys, dtypes, shard counts, sizes, and metadata headers needed to cross-check config consistency, never tensor payloads.
+- static model-card or registry metadata such as `README.md`, `model_index.json`, Hugging Face card `library_name`/`pipeline_tag`/`tags`, and exo model-card entries that record Pro as a text-only causal LM and not vision/audio/video/omnimodal capable.
+
+Expected tokenizer assets to inspect:
+
+- `tokenizer.json` or tokenizer model assets such as `tokenizer.model`, `vocab.json`, and `merges.txt`, depending on the upstream tokenizer format.
+- `tokenizer_config.json` for tokenizer class, chat template, model max length, normalization/pre-tokenization hints, and padding/truncation defaults.
+- `special_tokens_map.json` and any `added_tokens.json` for BOS/EOS/pad/UNK and additional special tokens required by text-only chat or agentic prompting.
+- Tokenizer metadata must be internally consistent with `config.json` and `generation_config.json`: special token IDs must agree across files, tokenizer max length must not silently exceed the validated long-context limit, and chat templates must accept text message content without requiring image, audio, video, or omnimodal placeholders.
+
+Expected config metadata to inspect:
+
+- `model_type`, `architectures`, and `auto_map` must identify a text-only causal LM path such as MiMo V2 causal LM metadata; they must not select a multimodal processor, vision tower, audio encoder, video adapter, or omnimodal wrapper.
+- Long-context fields such as `max_position_embeddings`, `rope_scaling`, `rope_theta`, sliding-window fields, and hybrid full/SWA attention fields must match the Track A text-core validation contract.
+- FP8 E4M3 and MoE fields must remain metadata-only validation inputs: quantization format/dtype, expert counts, routed/shared expert fields, top-k routing, hidden/intermediate sizes, layer counts, and any shard/index metadata needed to detect inconsistent declarations before loading weights.
+- MTP or next-token-prediction extension fields must be absent or explicitly disabled for this Track A slice.
+
+Required smoke-rung metadata fields/checks:
+
+- Text-only model identity: verify the requested/reported model identifier is exactly `XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5-Pro`, that exo registry/model-card metadata classifies it as `text-generation` or causal-LM style text generation only, and that any aliasing remains Pro-specific rather than affecting non-Pro models.
+- Tokenizer compatibility: verify tokenizer asset presence, tokenizer class/type, chat template compatibility with plain text messages, BOS/EOS/pad/UNK/additional special token declarations, token ID consistency across tokenizer/config/generation metadata, and tokenizer max length alignment with the validated Pro long-context limit.
+- Causal LM architecture hints: verify `architectures` includes a MiMo V2 causal LM class such as `MiMoV2ForCausalLM`, `model_type` identifies the MiMo V2 text model family, and `auto_map` entries, if present, point only at text causal-LM/tokenizer code paths rather than processors or media adapters.
+- Context-length fields: verify presence and coherence of long-context declarations such as `max_position_embeddings`, tokenizer `model_max_length`, `rope_theta`, `rope_scaling`, sliding-window size/enablement fields, and hybrid full/SWA attention layer-pattern fields. Inconsistent or missing long-context metadata for Pro must fail closed before model loading.
+- FP8/MoE/attention config presence: verify metadata-only presence of FP8 E4M3 quantization declarations, expected dtype/quantization format fields, MoE expert count/routing/shared-expert/top-k fields, layer/hidden/intermediate-size fields needed to cross-check MoE shape declarations, and hybrid attention fields needed to distinguish full attention from sliding-window attention.
+- Media capability absence: verify Pro metadata does not set or imply image, video, audio, multimodal, or omnimodal capability flags. Disallowed evidence includes media pipeline tags, processor classes, `vision_config`, `audio_config`, `video_config`, image/audio/video token placeholders in chat templates, vision towers, audio encoders, video adapters, omnimodal wrappers, or exo registry capability booleans set true for Pro.
+- Fail-closed result handling: any missing required text-core field, incompatible tokenizer/config mismatch, enabled MTP field, or media-bearing capability/request marker for Pro is a smoke-rung failure and must not fall through to weight materialization, MLX model construction, inference, or best-effort text fallback.
+
+### Pass signals
+
+The tokenizer/config inventory smoke rung passes only when all observed local metadata is complete compatible metadata for `XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5-Pro` as a text-only causal LM. A passing result requires:
+
+- All required lightweight metadata files are present locally, including `config.json`, tokenizer assets such as `tokenizer.json` or equivalent tokenizer vocabulary/model files, tokenizer configuration, special-token metadata when applicable, and any optional `generation_config.json` or repository index files that are already present in the prepared local directory.
