+## Dry request-guard validation smoke rung
+
+The dry request-guard validation smoke rung is a pre-dispatch, metadata-only request-shape check for `XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5-Pro`. It documents the accepted text-only Pro request shape and the rejected image request shapes, rejected video request shapes, rejected audio request shapes, and rejected omnimodal request shapes that must be refused before inference dispatch. This guard is intentionally dry: it parses only already-supplied request metadata and small in-process payload descriptors, and it must not tokenize prompts, instantiate processors, construct a model, load weights, allocate KV cache, schedule placement, create worker tasks, or call MLX inference.
+
+Accepted text-only Pro request shape:
+
+- The model identifier is exactly `XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5-Pro`; broad MiMo family aliases or non-Pro model identifiers do not enter this Pro-specific guard.
+- The user payload is plain text: either a plain string prompt, OpenAI-style chat messages whose `content` is a string, or structured chat content containing text content parts only.
+- Text content parts may carry only text fields such as `type: "text"`, `text`, `content`, role metadata, stop strings, sampling parameters, tool names/descriptions expressed as text, or agentic text fields used for planning/tool-call JSON. These fields must remain serializable text metadata, not binary blobs or URLs to media assets.
+- Long-context token budget metadata may be supplied as text-generation controls, for example max tokens, context-window intent, stop sequences, or truncation policy. The guard may record that such metadata must later be checked against Pro long-context config validation, but it must not tokenize or estimate with a loaded tokenizer in Track A.
+- A passing dry guard result records that the request is text-only, Pro-specific, and eligible to continue to later static model-card/config/placement checks; it does not by itself authorize inference or model loading.
+
+Rejected media-bearing Pro request shapes:
+
+- Rejected image request shapes include any `image`, `images`, `image_url`, `input_image`, `vision`, `vision_url`, image token placeholder, base64 image blob, image file path, image MIME type, vision processor hint, or visual-question-answering style content part.
+- Rejected video request shapes include any `video`, `videos`, `video_url`, `input_video`, video frame list, video file path, video MIME type, video adapter/decoder hint, video token placeholder, or text-to-video / video-text-to-text style request marker.
+- Rejected audio request shapes include any `audio`, `input_audio`, `audio_url`, `speech`, `voice`, waveform/base64 audio blob, audio file path, audio MIME type, audio encoder/decoder hint, ASR marker, text-to-audio marker, or audio token placeholder.
+- Rejected omnimodal request shapes include any `multimodal`, `omnimodal`, `modalities` containing image/video/audio, mixed content parts that combine text with media parts, processor payloads that accept media, generic attachment/file fields carrying media MIME types, or metadata that asks Pro to produce non-text output modalities.
+- Ambiguous request content that cannot be proven text-only from the supplied request metadata is unsupported for Track A. The guard must fail closed rather than stripping media fields, ignoring attachments, or attempting best-effort text extraction.
+
+Fail-closed behavior before inference dispatch:
+
+- Media-bearing Pro requests fail closed with explicit validation evidence and must stop before scheduler placement, must stop before worker task creation, must stop before tokenizer/model construction, and must stop before MLX inference dispatch.
+- The failure response should identify the first unsupported media marker or ambiguous request-shape reason when possible, while avoiding media decoding, remote fetches, artifact downloads, or payload inspection beyond lightweight metadata.
+- The guard must not create a best-effort text fallback by dropping media parts, converting captions, invoking processors, or forwarding only the textual subset of a mixed-media request. No best-effort text fallback is allowed for Pro media-bearing requests in Track A.
+- The guard is Pro-specific and must preserve existing model behavior for every non-`XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5-Pro` request. Non-Pro request validation, media-capable models, and existing runtime dispatch paths are outside this Track A scaffold.
+- A dry validation report should include request model ID, accepted/rejected status, text-only evidence for accepted requests, unsupported marker evidence for rejected requests, and an explicit no-side-effects statement: no downloads, no model loading, no processor loading, no tokenizer generation, no inference, no live `/Users/studio2/exo` mutation, and no runtime restart occurred.
