+## Dry scheduler/placement validation smoke rung
+
+The dry scheduler/placement validation smoke rung is a no-inference control-plane check for Pro placement eligibility. It validates whether already-known topology, node profiling, model-card, and request metadata would be eligible for a future text-only MLX placement, but it must not create an instance, download shards, start runners, instantiate tokenizers or models, allocate KV cache, load the giant Pro model, modify `/Users/studio2/exo`, restart services, or deploy anything live.
+
+This rung maps to the existing master placement surface without invoking live execution side effects: `src/exo/master/placement.py` considers `PlaceInstance` inputs, topology cycles, `MemoryUsage`, `NodeNetworkInfo`, requested sharding, model-card fields, and existing download-status summaries; `src/exo/master/placement_utils.py` computes memory filtering and shard-assignment shapes from metadata. A Track A dry run should exercise only equivalent pure validation over copied/static inputs and should return eligibility evidence rather than mutating `current_instances` or emitting worker tasks.
+
+Required node metadata inputs:
+
+- Topology cycle metadata for candidate nodes, including node IDs, graph connectivity, leaf-node status, and RDMA/socket edge metadata when `InstanceMeta.MlxJaccl` or ring placement constraints are being checked.
+- Per-node memory metadata from `MemoryUsage`, especially `ram_available`, sufficient for comparing against Pro model-card `storage_size` and for dry proportional layer allocation.
+- Per-node network metadata from `NodeNetworkInfo` only as static coordinator/ring eligibility input; the dry rung must not bind ports, open sockets, or start coordinators.
+- Optional existing download-status summaries may be read only as static `DownloadProgress` state for placement scoring; they must not trigger downloads, resume downloads, or inspect shard payloads.
+
+Required model and request metadata inputs:
+
+- The exact model identifier `XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.5-Pro`, a Pro-specific text-only model-card/registry entry, and no alias that changes non-Pro placement behavior.
+- Model-card fields used by placement and shard assignment: `storage_size`, `n_layers`, `hidden_size`, optional `num_key_value_heads`, `supports_tensor`, `uses_cfg`, and Track A text-only capability metadata.
+- Static config-validation evidence that Pro is a text-only `MiMoV2ForCausalLM` target with FP8 E4M3, MoE, hybrid full/SWA attention, long-context metadata, and MTP absent or explicitly disabled.
+- Request metadata limited to text-only placement intent: `PlaceInstance`/request model ID, `min_nodes`, `sharding`, `instance_meta`, required node set if present, and a request guard result proving no image, video, audio, multimodal, or omnimodal payload markers are present.
+
+Expected pass signals:
