+- Every candidate node used by the selected dry placement has memory metadata, and aggregate/proportional memory checks are sufficient for Pro `storage_size` and `n_layers` without allocating layers in a live instance.
+- Requested tensor sharding is allowed only when Pro model-card metadata explicitly supports tensor parallelism and divisibility checks such as `hidden_size % world_size == 0` and `num_key_value_heads % world_size == 0` pass when applicable.
+- Pipeline/ring dry assignment metadata can be derived from model-card fields and node memory without creating `Instance`, `MlxRingInstance`, `MlxJacclInstance`, `RunnerSupervisor`, worker tasks, downloads, or live network coordinators.
