+- Confirm the dry result either identifies candidate node IDs and a memory sufficiency summary or returns a fail-closed placement reason.
+- Confirm the check remains side-effect free: it must not mutate `current_instances`, emit `CreateInstance`, create worker tasks, open sockets, bind coordinators, resume downloads, allocate KV cache, load the giant Pro model, deploy anything live, or modify `/Users/studio2/exo`.
+- Treat any media-bearing Pro placement request as invalid even if the static topology and memory metadata would otherwise be sufficient.
+
+Expected evidence artifacts:
+
+- `pytest stdout` showing the three focused static test files above passed, plus any failure output when intentionally demonstrating a media rejection case.
+- `model-card-validation-report.json` when a future dry-run wrapper exists, containing at minimum `model_id`, `status`, `task_family`, `capabilities`, `no_downloads`, `no_model_loading`, `no_live_runtime_mutation`, and a list of absent/false media capability fields.
+- `dry-request-guard-report.json` when a future dry-run wrapper exists, containing at minimum `model_id`, `status`, `accepted_text_only` or `unsupported_media_marker`, `stopped_before`, `no_downloads`, `no_model_loading`, and `no_live_runtime_mutation`.
+- `dry-placement-report.json` when a future dry-run wrapper exists, containing at minimum `model_id`, `status`, `candidate_node_ids`, `memory_sufficiency_summary`, `request_guard_status`, `stopped_before` for failures, `no_downloads`, `no_model_loading`, and `no_live_runtime_mutation`.
+- For Track A documentation-only review, these JSON artifacts may be represented as expected schemas/examples in docs or tests; they are not required to be produced by a live runtime.
+
